      "Language": "fre",
      "Abstract": {"AbstractText": "The clinical, electrocardiographic, coronarographic and hemodynamic findings in thirty-one patients with left coronary artery stenosis were compared with those noted in patients with critical stenoses in all the three branches only. It was not possible to distinguish between the two groups of patients by comparing these results, and coronary arteriography is still the only valid diagnostic procedure."},
